From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] apklayer: native-surface-parcel

apklayer patch: Surface.nativeReadFromParcel / nativeWriteToParcel / nativeGetFromSurfaceControl are the real natives. Upstream
stubbed them (read and new Surface(SurfaceControl) gave no surface, write wrote nothing), so a Surface sent to another app process through a binder call (GeckoView's GPU process gets its
compositor Surface this way) arrived as no window: ANativeWindow_fromSurface gave null. nativeCreateFromSurfaceTexture is real too: the
stub made new Surface(SurfaceTexture) a released Surface, so a video decoder given one failed (MediaCodec.configure: "The surface has been released").

Against external/robolectric 87aa52b08 (REVISION). Applied by runtime/meson.build onto the staged upstream sources
(<native>/aosp/robolectric-src); the result is compiled into native-runtime.jar ahead of Robolectric_all.jar.
---
diff --git a/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowNativeSurface.java b/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowNativeSurface.java
--- a/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowNativeSurface.java
+++ b/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowNativeSurface.java
@@ -48,12 +48,8 @@
   // the ImageReader.OnImageAvailableListener callback and drawing.
   private final AtomicReference<ImageReader> containerImageReader = new AtomicReference<>(null);

-  @Implementation
-  protected static long nativeCreateFromSurfaceTexture(SurfaceTexture surfaceTexture)
-      throws OutOfResourcesException {
-    // SurfaceTexture is not available for host.
-    return 0;
-  }
+  // apklayer patch: nativeCreateFromSurfaceTexture is the real native: SurfaceTexture is real here (a BufferQueue and GLConsumer), and a Surface
+  // made from it (new Surface(surfaceTexture), the output of a video decoder) is its producer; the stub gave a released Surface

   @Implementation(maxSdk = UPSIDE_DOWN_CAKE)
   protected static long nativeCreateFromSurfaceControl(long surfaceControlNativeObject) {
@@ -61,15 +57,12 @@
     return SurfaceNatives.nativeCreateFromSurfaceControl(surfaceControlNativeObject);
   }
 
-  @Implementation(minSdk = Q)
-  protected static long nativeGetFromSurfaceControl(
-      long surfaceObject, long surfaceControlNativeObject) {
-    return 0;
-  }
+  // apklayer patch: nativeGetFromSurfaceControl (Q+) is the real native: a Surface made from a SurfaceControl (new Surface(SurfaceControl),
+  // GeckoView's child surfaces) is the SurfaceControl's BLAST surface; the stub gave none
 
   @Implementation(minSdk = P, maxSdk = P)
   protected static long nativeGetFromSurfaceControl(long surfaceControlNativeObject) {
-    return nativeGetFromSurfaceControl(0, surfaceControlNativeObject);
+    return 0;
   }
 
   @Implementation(minSdk = S, maxSdk = UPSIDE_DOWN_CAKE)
@@ -105,14 +98,9 @@
     return SurfaceNatives.nativeIsConsumerRunningBehind(nativeObject);
   }
 
-  @Implementation
-  protected static long nativeReadFromParcel(long nativeObject, Parcel source) {
-    return 0;
-  }
+  // apklayer patch: nativeReadFromParcel and nativeWriteToParcel are the real natives (a Surface sent to another app process stays a window: its
+  // IGraphicBufferProducer crosses in the binder Parcel; the stubs here returned no surface and wrote nothing)
 
-  @Implementation
-  protected static void nativeWriteToParcel(long nativeObject, Parcel dest) {}
-
   @Implementation(maxSdk = UPSIDE_DOWN_CAKE)
   protected static void nativeAllocateBuffers(long nativeObject) {
     SurfaceNatives.nativeAllocateBuffers(nativeObject);
